https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gdm/-/commit/174f77ce3f046e99c67183175bc840c3a62fec6e

Upstream's own fix for the GDM_AUTH_SESSION_ID regression (commit
6bee0c43b2, "session: Set GDM_AUTH_SESSION_ID env var for PAM
conversations", included in the 51.beta tarball) that this overlay
previously carried its own local revert patch for. Adopt the official
fix instead of the local revert now that it exists upstream.

From 174f77ce3f046e99c67183175bc840c3a62fec6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Torres Lopez <joantolo@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 10:58:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] session-worker: Fix wrong pam_putenv of GDM_AUTH_SESSION_ID

GDM_AUTH_SESSION_ID is passed via setenv(), not pam_putenv(), and it's unset
with unsetenv(), there's no need to unset it with pam_putenv() because
it hasn't been set with it in the first place.

Fixes: 6bee0c43b2 ("session: Set GDM_AUTH_SESSION_ID env var for PAM
conversations")
---
 daemon/gdm-session-worker.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c b/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
index 655e5ed9f..1a6b1bf59 100644
--- a/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
@@ -1429,7 +1429,6 @@ gdm_session_worker_authenticate_user (GdmSessionWorker *worker,
                 goto out;
         }

-        gdm_session_worker_set_environment_variable (worker, GDM_AUTH_SESSION_ID, NULL);
         unsetenv (GDM_AUTH_SESSION_ID);

         g_debug ("GdmSessionWorker: state AUTHENTICATED");
--
GitLab
